","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:8d5d383a5b61706cb4cc6353dad5b3a90a36fc8587b4f999ff84e7202a61341a","file":"preprints/Global-Support-and-Convex-Injectivity-Domains-under-Weak-MTW-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":47,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"f861bc58b2840a9c256c13a1cab27edca182c68552091f48f464f8687256aa9e","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Global-Support-and-Convex-Injectivity-Domains-under-Weak-MTW-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:8d5d383a5b61706cb4cc6353dad5b3a90a36fc8587b4f999ff84e7202a61341a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Global-Support-and-Convex-Injectivity-Domains-under-Weak-MTW-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L47"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nIf $(M,g)$ satisfies \\eqref{eq:weak-mtw}, then $I(x)$ is convex for\nevery $x\\in M$. More precisely, for every $v_0,v_1\\in I(x)$ and\n$\\theta\\in[0,1]$,\n\\[\n (1-\\theta)v_0+\\theta v_1\\in I(x).\n\\]"}
